        },
        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*A grey-bearded man in war-worn mail looks up from his ale and measures you with a soldier's eye.* Hallas, once of the Guard of Gondor -- folk hereabouts call me the Shieldwarden. You carry yourself like one who has stood in a shield-wall, or means to. There is an old oath the men-at-arms of the West still swear -- the oath of the Unbroken Shield: to hold the line when the line would break, and to stand for those who cannot stand. Will you swear it, and let me set your feet on a soldier's road?"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "__struct_id": 1,
        "Animation": {
          "type": "dword",
          "value": 0
        },
        "AnimLoop": {
          "type": "byte",
          "value": 1
        },
        "Comment": {
          "type": "cexostring",
          "value": ""
        },
        "Delay": {
          "type": "dword",
          "value": 4294967295
        },
        "Quest": {
          "type": "cexostring",
          "value": ""
        },
        "RepliesList": {
          "type": "list",
          "value": [
            {
              "__struct_id": 0,
              "Active": {
                "type": "resref",
                "value": ""
              },
              "Index": {
                "type": "dword",
                "value": 6
              },
              "IsChild": {
                "type": "byte",
                "value": 0
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "Script": {
          "type": "resref",
